{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310782,"nonce":"QQTW0JMvbxyB2qQnYTSjTEG4/UE=","title":"Cranelift FMA fusion landscape post-8394d20 (2026-06-06): scalar FMA peephole (instruction_lowering.rs) has been in place since some ...","message":"| Location | Path | Status |\n|---|---|---|\n| Scalar `BinaryOp::Add` (FP) | `instruction_lowering.rs:124` | ✅ FMA fusion (pre-existing) |\n| Scalar `BinaryOp::Sub` (FP) | `instruction_lowering.rs:138` | ✅ FMS fusion via fneg + fma |\n| Scalar `BinaryOp::FAdd` | `instruction_lowering.rs:201` | ✅ FMA fusion |\n| Scalar `BinaryOp::FSub` | `instruction_lowering.rs:210` | ✅ FMS fusion via fneg + fma |\n| Static `lower_binary_op_static` | `instruction_lowering.rs:564+` | ✅ Same coverage as the instance method |\n| Vector `VectorBinOp::Add/FAdd` | `cranelift_backend.rs:4113` | ✅ Landed 8394d20 |\n| Vector `VectorBinOp::Sub/FSub` | `cranelift_backend.rs:4135` | ✅ Landed 8394d20 |\n| Vector `VectorReduce` | `cranelift_backend.rs:4212+` | ❌ Not fused (reduction tree only) |\n\n\nBoth helpers (`try_extract_fmul`, `try_extract_vector_fmul`) enforce:\n\n1. **Same-block restriction.** Cross-block fusion would change FP\n   semantics for values that originally went through memory\n   (store/load), since SROA + CopyProp can expose fmul results across\n   block boundaries that were previously hidden by memory operations.\n\n2. **`RAYZOR_NO_FMA=1` escape hatch.** Disables fusion globally on\n   both scalar and vector paths.\n\n\n\n```\nFMA on:   0.97s 0.97s 0.97s  → median 0.97s\nFMA off:  0.98s 0.98s 0.99s  → median 0.98s\n```\n\n~1-2% wall, consistent (3-0 sign test). Small because nbody's wall is\ndominated by binary startup (~0.5s); the actual compute portion gets\nmaybe 3-5%. Matches the typical FMA win (one fused issue vs\nfmul+fadd).\n\n\n```\n30.605 tok/s median, σ=0.4, range 29.87-30.80 (clean 5/5 runs)\n```\n\nNo regression. The matmul kernels are in `runtime/` written as Rust\nNEON intrinsics — they don't go through Cranelift, so the FMA\npeephole doesn't affect them. The win surfaces only in Haxe-side\narithmetic, which is a small fraction of decode wall.\n\n\nRayzor's hot paths are:\n- `runtime/src/quant.rs` matmul kernels (NEON intrinsics, scalar Rust\n  with `target_feature(enable = \"neon\")` / hand-vectorised)\n- `runtime/src/tensor.rs` flash attention, RMSNorm, etc. (NEON via\n  `tensor_simd` helpers)\n- `runtime/src/tensor_simd.rs` `dot_slice_f32`, `axpy_slice` (NEON +\n  SSE specialisations)\n\nNone of these are touched by Cranelift. The Haxe-side code is\nmostly orchestration: tensor view construction, the per-token\ngeneration loop, sampling, tokenizer. Inner FP arithmetic in those\npaths is rare.\n\n\n1. **`nbody.hx` and other Haxe benchmarks** that do `a*b+c` patterns\n   in pure-Haxe loops without offloading to runtime kernels.\n2. **GPU compute kernels via KernelIR** — the WGSL/MSL/CUDA codegen\n   paths get `mad` / `fma` for free from their respective shading\n   languages, but the lazy-fusion intermediate form goes through MIR.\n3. **WASM SIMD lowering** — the wasm_backend reads VectorBinOp +\n   VectorReduce; fusing here propagates to WebAssembly `f32x4.qfma`\n   (still proposal at writing).\n4. **Vector8f / VectorOps** explicit Haxe-side SIMD math — used by\n   demo apps, future ML kernels in pure Haxe, custom DSL targets.\n\n\n- **`VectorReduce` FMA fusion**: the reduction tree at\n  `cranelift_backend.rs:4212+` does `extractlane` + scalar\n  `fadd`/`fmul` in a loop. Each loop body could fuse if a preceding\n  fmul fed the accumulator. Niche; probably \u003c0.5% on real workloads.\n\n- **Cross-block fusion with SROA-awareness**: track which fmul\n  results were originally memory-mediated and skip those; allow\n  same-function cross-block fusion otherwise. Multi-session work,\n  uncertain win. Most loops with FMA opportunities have the fmul +\n  fadd in the same block already (loop bodies don't fission casually).\n\n- **`Fadd(Fmul(x, c1), c2)` where c1, c2 are constants**: peephole\n  to constant-fold the scalar before fusing. Probably already done by\n  Cranelift's egraph layer.\n\n- **`-fneg(a*b + c) → fma(-a, b, c)` canonicalisation**: would help\n  computations with explicit sign-negation around an FMA. Tiny niche.\n\n\n- The scalar fusion comments in `instruction_lowering.rs` mention\n  this codebase has historical context for the same-block restriction\n  (SROA + CopyProp interactions). See [[bugs-w0020-value-map-miss-cross-loop]]\n  and [[project-compiler-ssa-hygiene-followups]] for the SSA hygiene\n  arc that surfaced these constraints.\n- 8394d20 — vector FMA peephole landing commit.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `perf_cranelift_fma_landscape` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}